    "country": "US",
    "date": "2026-08-20",
    "title": "More Than Dog Food",
    "text": "More Than Dog Food — A Team That Showed Us Genuine Compassion\n\nI originally came back to The Farmer’s Dog because of my 15-year-old dog, Asahi, whom we also call Bubbles.\n\nOver the past year, Bubbles has been through more than I ever imagined an old little dog could endure — pancreatitis, a colon infection, Giardia, gallbladder problems, popped eye lens caused by Glaucoma and all the complications that can come with being 15 years old. At his worst, his weight dropped from around 10 pounds to only 4–4.5 pounds. There were moments when nobody thought he was going to make it.\n\nSomehow, slowly, he recovered.\n\nBut after everything his body had been through, eating became incredibly difficult. He became extremely picky and selective, and every meal became something I worried about. I decided to try The Farmer’s Dog again, simply hoping it might be one of the foods he would still accept.\n\nThen came another very bad week. Bubbles refused everything I offered him. Chicken. Different brands of dog food. I was so desperate that I even tried Spam just hoping he would eat something. Nothing worked.\n\nThen I put down a plate of The Farmer’s Dog.\n\nHe ate the entire thing.\n\nI cried.\n\nAfter spending so much time watching him struggle, seeing him actually want food again felt like the smallest little light at the end of an incredibly long tunnel.\n\nI emailed The Farmer’s Dog simply because I wanted to share what that moment meant to me. I wasn’t expecting anything in return. The next day, Melanie from their support team called me and left the most heartfelt voicemail, and she followed up with an email offering encouragement and support. It genuinely touched me.\n\nBubbles began feeling better again for a while.\n\nUnfortunately, this week he has declined again. He has been dealing with diarrhea and refusing food, and at 15 years old, I understand the reality that his time with us is precious and limited.\n\nI already had another Farmer’s Dog shipment scheduled and reached out hoping I could cancel it. I didn’t realize it had already shipped and was on its way.\n\nTheir response left me emotional all over again.\n\nThey refunded the order anyway and told me that when the food arrived, I could share it with friends, family, or another dog in need. Dylan also sent another incredibly kind and supportive message during what has been a very difficult and uncertain time for me.\n\nAt this stage of Bubbles’ life, it isn’t just about dog food anymore.\n\nWhen you love an animal for 15 years, they become part of your identity, your routines, your family, and your heart. Knowing that his days may be numbered is incredibly painful. Sometimes a little compassion from another person can mean far more than they realize.\n\nThe Farmer’s Dog team gave me that compassion — twice.\n\nI will never forget the day Bubbles refused everything except their food, and I will never forget how their team treated us when we were struggling.\n\nThank you to Melanie and Dylan and everyone at The Farmer’s Dog for seeing the person and the little old dog behind an order number. Your kindness helped me through some very dark days.\n\nAnd from Bubbles — thank you for giving an old, stubborn, very loved little dog a meal he actually wanted to eat. ❤️",
